Build the Windows installer on GitHub for the commit tagged `build`

Purpose:
Get an installable Windows build without building locally, for exactly
the commits that should be built: pushing the tag `build` (moved with
`git overlay-build`) builds the NSIS installer and publishes it at a
fixed URL.

Approach:
- .github/workflows/overlay-windows-build.yml at the repo root (only root
  workflows run in the monorepo), on windows-latest, triggered by pushes
  of the tag `build`.
- No versioning: one prerelease on the `build` tag. Each run deletes it
  (keeping the tag) and recreates it with the installer as
  Gingko-Writer-Setup.exe, so the download link
  releases/download/build/Gingko-Writer-Setup.exe never changes.
- `bun install --ignore-scripts` skips the Electron download and
  node-pty's native build, which only the web/Electron tooling needs;
  Elm 0.19.1 is therefore fetched as a standalone binary (ELM_BINARY)
  instead of via the npm package's install script.
- Rust (Swatinem/rust-cache) and Elm packages (elm-home) are cached; a
  newer tag push cancels a running build.

Constraints:
- Windows NSIS installer only; unsigned (SmartScreen warns on first run).
- Doesn't touch upstream's workflows (web-deploy.yml runs only on
  master, on upstream's self-hosted runner).

